deep:[["Routing between servers","Each gateway registers user → gateway in Redis on connect. The chat service looks up the recipient and forwards to that gateway (direct RPC or a per-gateway pub/sub channel). If absent → offline path."],["Ordering","Order within a chat by a server-assigned, per-chat increasing ID (Snowflake or a per-chat sequence). Clients sort by it, and dedupe retried sends with client_msg_id."],["Storage","Wide-column store partitioned by chat_id (plus a time bucket for huge chats), clustered by message_id desc → 'latest 50' is one partition read."],["Offline delivery and receipts","Messages persist before ack. On reconnect the client sends its last seen message_id per chat and pulls the gap. Delivered/read receipts are just small messages back to the sender."],["Groups","Fan-out on write to each member's gateway for groups up to ~200. Very large broadcast channels switch to fan-out on read."],["Presence","Heartbeats every ~30 s update last_seen in Redis with TTL; publish presence changes only to contacts who are online and subscribed, and throttle it."]],
